{
  "version": 2,
  "note": "Markers of the Captain Pack map (core/captain_map.gd, ui/menu/captain_map_panel.gd). x, y = position on the picture, 0..1 of its width and height; a marker without x and y is not visible in the photo and sits in a strip under it. A marker is one physical control; its parts are the positions or keys it has (id unique in the marker). A part's pad number comes from `key` (a default action of InputProfiles.captain_pack: the numbers are never typed twice), or `axis` / `button` here, or nothing when the number is unknown. conf = measured (seen on the owner's pack), documented (a public source, see sources) or unconfirmed (guessed or unknown: the panel's Identify mode settles it and saves the correction to user://captain_map_learned.json). flip = lever forward reads falling. latching = a switch that stays down. check = group of CaptainCheck.GROUPS (what to move to test it). unmapped = pad buttons that are not keys (virtual zone buttons of the levers).",
  "sources": {
    "capture": "Measured on the owner's pack on macOS, 2026-11-04 and 05 (core/input_profiles.gd, docs/USAGE.md).",
    "tomvand": "Community X-Plane button list of the TCA Q-Eng 1&2 (github.com/tomvand/xp-thrustmaster-tca). It counts from 1, so 1 is subtracted; it agrees with every number measured on the quadrant.",
    "hat": "libresim note in core/input_profiles.gd: buttons 11-14 are the hat. Which of 13 and 14 is left or right was not checked.",
    "none": "No public source found: press the key with Identify on."
  },
